---
/**
 * "How I work" — cómo un repositorio de apuntes acabó siendo MLabs.
 *
 * ⚠️ Reescrita como HISTORIA, 2026-09-04. La versión anterior eran cuatro
 * secciones temáticas y abría con una lista ("tres cosas me frenaban"); una
 * lista no se sigue como una historia y no se dibuja.
 *
 * La forma: cada escena resuelve algo Y plantea el problema que su propio
 * éxito creó. Eso es lo que la separa de una cronología, y es lo que hace que
 * el enlace a MLabs al final esté GANADO en vez de anunciado.
 *
 * Reparto con la ficha de MLabs (AX-20, el mismo hecho no vive en dos sitios):
 * aquí el RECORRIDO y los ficheros de proyecto; allí los tres bloques, el
 * bucle de sesión y las cláusulas de filosofía.
 *
 * Presupuesto AX-9: 3 figuras = 36 s, quedan ~204 s de texto.
 */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import StoryArc from "../../components/figures/StoryArc.astro";
import ProjectCartridge from "../../components/figures/ProjectCartridge.astro";
import PermissionTable from "../../components/figures/PermissionTable.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/url";
import { LINKS } from "../../consts";
---

<Base
  title="How I work"
  description="How a folder of study notes turned into a knowledge base, then a way of running projects, and finally a published methodology with its own rules."
>
  <article class="closer">
    <div class="container closer__wrap">
      <a class="closer__back" href={withBase("/#how-title")}>← Back to how I work</a>

      <header class="closer__header">
        <span class="mono-label">How I work · how it got built</span>
        <h1>It started as a folder of notes</h1>
        <p class="closer__lede">
          None of it was designed up front: each piece exists because the
          previous one worked well enough to create a new problem.
        </p>
      </header>

      <StoryArc />

      <div class="closer__walk">
        <!-- Escena 1 -->
        <section class="closer__phase reveal">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">A system that remembers for me</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            I began saving summaries and notes from what I studied into a
            repository, so I wouldn't lose them. It grew into my whole master's
            as linked notes across eight domains.
          </p>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            <strong>And then it stopped being enough.</strong> A knowledge base
            answers <em>what do I know about this?</em> — never <em>what do I do
            on Monday?</em>
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Escena 2 -->
        <section class="closer__phase reveal">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">Then the projects moved in</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            So the projects came to live beside the knowledge they draw on, and
            each new one starts from what is there rather than nothing.
          </p>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            <strong>Which created the next problem.</strong> Several running at
            once, and no way to tell where any stood without rebuilding it from
            memory every time I came back.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Escena 3 · la que más vende -->
        <section class="closer__phase reveal">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">A record someone else could pick up</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            Every project keeps a small set of files, and each answers a
            question the others don't — and that version control can't. Git
            records what changed and when, never why, who decided it, or what
            was rejected: a rejected approach is never written down at all.
          </p>

          <ProjectCartridge />

          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            That is what turned AI from an assistant into something doing real
            work here. An agent opens the project, reads what is true today and
            what was already decided, and starts — without me rebuilding the
            context in a prompt.
          </p>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            Which only works if it is safe. Write access is decided per artifact,
            and the gate is on the agent's <em>initiative</em>, not its hands:
            what it concludes on its own goes to a mailbox, and I integrate it or
            I don't.
          </p>

          <PermissionTable />
        </section>

        <!-- Escena 4 · el traspaso a MLabs -->
        <section class="closer__phase reveal">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">So the method got rules of its own</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            By then the way of working was a thing in its own right, and it kept
            growing. Anything that grows without rules collapses under itself, so
            I wrapped it in some: roles that answer for what they do, checks
            proven to fire, and a philosophy that decides when two rules
            disagree.
          </p>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            It is a separate project now, published so that whether it works for
            anyone but me is a question somebody can answer rather than a claim I
            get to make.
          </p>

          <a class="closer__pointer" href={withBase("/work/mlabs")}>
            <span class="mono-label">Where it ends up</span>
            <span class="closer__pointer-title">
              MLabs — the store, the method, and the philosophy that keeps it
              from breaking
              <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </section>
      </div>

      <p class="closer__outro">
        Still under construction, and always will be: a system that stops
        changing has stopped being used.{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>Ask me about any of it</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .closer {
    padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-2xl);
    /* AX-12 · atmósfera de capítulo en el suelo; el acento no se toca. */
    --ground-2: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-deep) 6%, var(--paper));
    --ground-tint: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-deep) 9%, var(--paper));
    --ground-rule: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-deep) 32%, var(--line));
  }
  .closer__wrap {
    max-width: 54rem;
  }
  .closer__back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .closer__header {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: var(--border);
  }
  .closer__header h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }
  .closer__lede {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* El arco va antes del recorrido y con aire propio: es el índice visual de
     lo que viene, no la primera sección. */
  .closer__walk {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }
  .closer__walk > * {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .closer__phase-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 30%, transparent);
  }
  .closer__phase-intro {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }
  .closer__phase-intro + :global(figure) {
    margin-top: calc(var(--space-lg) * -1 + var(--space-md));
  }
  :global(figure) + .closer__phase-intro {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .closer__phase-intro strong {
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }

  .closer__pointer {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, var(--line));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 7%, var(--paper));
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease),
      border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }
  .closer__pointer:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 13%, var(--paper));
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .closer__pointer-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  /* La flecha va en su propio span y Astro se come el salto de línea que la
     precede. Se resuelve en CSS y no con un espacio explícito porque aquí el
     contenedor no es flex — un margen sobrevive a la siguiente reescritura del
     texto, y un {" "} no. */
  .closer__pointer-title span {
    margin-left: 0.35em;
  }

  .closer__outro {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: var(--border);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }
</style>
